From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 19:39:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libfetch: check the result of SSL_CTX_new()

SSL_CTX_new() returns NULL on allocation failure or if the method is
unusable, and the very next statement passes the result to
SSL_CTX_set_mode(), which dereferences it.

Fail via the existing err label, which reports FETCH_ERR_TLS.  The
matching SSL_new() call a few lines below is already checked this way.

Signed-off-by: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
---
 libfetch/common.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/libfetch/common.c b/libfetch/common.c
index 3c09f6d..edc2f52 100644
--- a/libfetch/common.c
+++ b/libfetch/common.c
@@ -509,6 +509,7 @@ fetch_ssl(conn_t *conn, const struct url *URL, int verbose)
 	conn->ssl_meth = TLS_client_method();
 #endif
 	conn->ssl_ctx = SSL_CTX_new(conn->ssl_meth);
+	if (conn->ssl_ctx == NULL) goto err;
 	SSL_CTX_set_mode(conn->ssl_ctx, SSL_MODE_AUTO_RETRY);
 
 	if (!fetch_ssl_setup_peer_verification(conn->ssl_ctx, verbose)) goto err;
